# The source of `.env.mcp`, which `scripts/deploy.sh` generates: this file with
# the MCP servers' tokens from SSM (BRAVE_API_KEY, ARGOCD_API_TOKEN) appended.
# Addresses and accounts that belong to individual MCP servers go here, in git;
# `.env.mcp` itself is overwritten on every run.
#
# Everything below belongs to the `eks` profile. These three servers reached
# their targets over cluster DNS; from this host each needs an address that
# resolves publicly, and until one exists adding `eks` to COMPOSE_PROFILES
# gives them nothing to point at.

# mcp-argocd
ARGOCD_BASE_URL=

# mcp-grafana — basic auth with the same credentials that seed Grafana's own
# admin user, not a service account token: a token lives in Grafana's database
# and dies with the PVC.
#
# The credentials are **not** here. SSM holds them (/k8s/common/admin-user,
# /k8s/common/admin-password) and deploy.sh should take them the way it takes
# every other secret — but that needs agentdure-idc-ssm-read widened past
# /k8s/common/agentdure/* and /k8s/common/mcp-*, which puts the cluster's Grafana
# admin password behind this host's access key. Worth doing when the profile is
# actually wired up; not worth doing for a profile that cannot run.
#
# Only the address is a person's to type, and only because SSM has no parameter
# for it. ArgoCD's does exist (/k8s/common/argocd-hostname), so that one moves to
# deploy.sh at the same time.
GRAFANA_URL=
